      "role": "user",
      "content": "That's a decent start. It's definitely more polished than my notes, but it feels a little light on the \"sensory\" side—the editor is actually being kind of stickler about that richness score. They want the description to feel \"lush\" and \"vibrant\" to justify the high-end price point of the bistro. \n\nCould you try expanding it a bit? Make it more evocative and \"rich\" so we get a better score from the tool, but I'm serious—don't let it turn into a word salad. I just want it to feel more high-end and textured without losing the actual critique about the salt and the service speed.",
      "source": "evaluator"
